diff --git a/HORDE_REFEREE.md b/HORDE_REFEREE.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a1a4234
--- /dev/null
+++ b/HORDE_REFEREE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+# Horde referee contract
+
+This patch is based on `AndyGrant/cutechess` commit
+`24d4301152fb92ac442425e083a2658225f80720`. Horde rules and game outcomes are
+matched to `lichess-org/scalachess` commit
+`d5d47c16f65a005ca68e19bab702b02f66dd888c`.
+
+The referee implements the following Horde-specific contract:
+
+- White has no king and Black has exactly one king.
+- Only Black may castle.
+- A White pawn may move two squares from the first or second rank. A move from
+  the first to the third rank does not grant an en-passant capture.
+- Terminal precedence is checkmate, Horde extinction, stalemate, closed Horde
+  position, fifty-move draw, then fivefold repetition.
+- Classical insufficient-material and automatic threefold-repetition draws do
+  not apply.
+- `HordeBoard::sideHasInsufficientWinningMaterial()` exposes the side-specific
+  winning-material predicate used by the timeout path.
+- `HordeBoard::winPossible()` evaluates winning material and the closed-position
+  predicate independently before a timeout is scored.
+
+## Pinned validation data
+
+`projects/lib/tests/data/horde_insufficient_material.csv` is copied byte for
+byte from the pinned scalachess test kit:
+
+- Rows: `21,996`
+- SHA-256: `1F01B4FD3AB6066EFE5A96A2AE4E0DF5074FB99377D7CAAA2ACBA04D453D53CC`
+
+The native board test also checks Horde terminal ordering, both stalemate
+directions, closed and breakable fortresses, timeout capability for each side,
+last-piece capture, first-rank en passant, Black-only castling, fivefold
+repetition, and the canonical Fairy-Stockfish perfts.
+
+## Headless build
+
+```sh
+cmake -S . -B build -DWITH_GUI=OFF -DWITH_TESTS=ON -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
+cmake --build build --target test_chessboard cli
+ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
+```
+
+For a deployable static CLI, add `-DWITH_STATIC_RUNTIME=ON` and point
+`CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH` at a static Qt 5 installation. When Qt 6 is also installed,
+add `-DCMAKE_DISABLE_FIND_PACKAGE_Qt6=TRUE` to select Qt 5 explicitly.
+
+The C language mode is pinned to C17 because the bundled Fathom source defines
+its own `bool` type and is not compatible with a compiler defaulting to C23.
+
+## Upstream control
+
+On Windows with GCC 16.1.0 and Qt 5.15.19, all 35 Horde-focused cases pass.
+The complete chessboard suite reports 301 passes and one unrelated pre-existing
+failure: `grid pos2` produces `1,853,380` nodes instead of the stored
+`1,853,429`. A clean checkout of the unmodified base commit produces the same
+result with the same toolchain.
